# Rich Text Editors & Excalidraw

## Three Editors

Brainitive uses three different rich text editors for different contexts:

### 1. Editor.js (`@editorjs/editorjs`)
- Used for structured block-based content
- Component: `resources/js/components/editor/EditorJS.tsx`
- Plugins: header, list, nested-list, checklist, code, delimiter, embed, image, link, marker, inline-code, paragraph, quote, raw, table, text-variant-tune, underline, warning, attaches, alert, drag-drop, undo
- File uploads via `FileController` to public disk

### 2. Tiptap 3 (`@tiptap/react`)
- Used for rich page editing with advanced features
- Extensions: starter-kit, bubble-menu, floating-menu, code-block-lowlight, color, heading, highlight, horizontal-rule, image, link, mention, placeholder, table (with cells/header/row), task-item/list, text-align, text-style, typography, underline, suggestion
- Custom extensions in `resources/js/components/editor/extensions/`

### 3. Lexical (`@lexical/react`)
- Used for advanced document editing
- Components: `LexicalEditor.tsx`, `RichLexicalEditor.tsx`, `RichLexicalEditorFull.tsx`
- Features: clipboard, code highlighting, hashtag, HTML import/export, link, list, markdown shortcuts, overflow, rich-text, selection, table
- Custom nodes in `resources/js/components/editor/nodes/`
- Custom plugins in `resources/js/components/editor/plugins/`

### 4. Excalidraw (`@excalidraw/excalidraw`)
- Whiteboard/diagramming tool embedded in pages
- Pages can be of type "whiteboard" (detected via `is_whiteboard` appended attribute)
- Excalidraw data stored as JSON in page `content` field
- Standalone build in `excalidraw-build/` for a separate bundle
- Blade template: `excalidraw-editor.blade.php`

## Content Storage

- Editor content is stored as JSON in the database (`content` column, cast as `array`)
- File attachments uploaded to `public` disk with UUID filenames
- Images uploaded via `FileController` (`/upload/image`, `/upload/file`)

## Editor Component Patterns

```tsx
// Using a Tiptap editor
import { useEditor, EditorContent } from '@tiptap/react';
import StarterKit from '@tiptap/starter-kit';

const editor = useEditor({
    extensions: [StarterKit, /* other extensions */],
    content: initialContent,
    onUpdate: ({ editor }) => {
        // Save content
    },
});
```

## Slash Commands

- Available in Tiptap via `SlashCommands.tsx`
- Triggered by typing `/` in the editor
- Commands include: headings, lists, code blocks, images, embeds, Excalidraw
